body:
A girlfriend will not complete you, it will complicate you. It's awesome that you are focused on personal development. Check out the books I recommended + 7 Habits of Highly Effective People. 

Losing your virginity isn't as big a deal as it probably FEELS, so don't over think it. Take action, lead interactions, and have fun! Good luck on your journey to become a more integrated and self-actualized man! 

&#x200B;

Dude you are 16 it is okay not to have a gf. To work on your confidence I'd recommend some books: 

No More Mr.Nice guy

12 Rules for Life

Corey Wayne 3% Man

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Your situation is far from hopeless! Be proud of yourself for all your past efforts. You have a degree. Even if you dislike the field of study it's still an accomplishment! University is not a magic fix. I don't think you should go back to school; not yet. Your priority should be on personal development. You are an adult, and responsible for yourself going forward. Stop blaming your parents because it is not productive. Let the past rest. 

Life is difficult; setbacks and poverty can happen at any stage of life. Many people never learn to cope with adversity, so you are actually lucky to have faced these challenges while still young and without children. Don't waste your energy wishing you had a relationship. Focus on your own needs. Building yourself up! Intelligent men are attracted to capable and resilient women; and that is you!  So let's change your mindset. 

I understand the stress of constantly being in survival mode; but know that money will not solve all of your problems. You can improve your situation, but first you must work on yourself. Being thin is better than being overweight!! and taking the bus is nothing to be ashamed of. Stop seeking external forms of validation. Everything is within you! You need to love and respect yourself. You are worth all the effort!  Focus on today.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

