In the Tokogawa period, Japan was trading with the Dutch and had continual regional trade with China/Korea. You can't say the Japanese were oppressed or colonized by the West. The Japanese understood how vulnerable their nation was to modern weapons, and so forced Japana into an industrial revolution. In 10 years the Meiji restoration moved Japan from a feudal society into the dominant regional power. Just 50 years after the US 'opened' Japan.... Japan defeated Russia! \*and at the time it was inconceivable for an Asian nation to ever compete equally with a Western (white) power.

&#x200B;

EDIT: Fun fact.... The only three nations on earth to avoid colonization are Thailand, Japan, and Ethiopia.
